<title>UK: PREMIER, HESS IN UK N. SEA OIL DISCOVERY.</title>
<headline>PREMIER, HESS IN UK N. SEA OIL DISCOVERY.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. oil company Amerada Hess Corp and its joint venture partner Premier Oil plc have discovered a &quot;potentially commercial&quot; oil accumulation on Block 31/26a in the central North Sea, near the Hess-operated Fife field, Hess said on Monday.</p>
<p>In a statement, Hess said the exploration well on the block successfully tests at a stabilised rate of 6,500 barrels of oil a day of 34 API oil through a 28/62 inch choke.</p>
<p>&quot;Studies are now progressing to enable development of this discovery by means of a tie-back to Fife,&quot; Hess said.</p>
<p>Hess has an 85 percent stake in the venture and Premier a 15 percent stake.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom, +44 171 542 7717</p>
